    "TS-KURA-PDP-COVER-VID": {
      "platform": [
        "linkedin",
        "instagram"
      ],
      "assetType": "video",
      "assetUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/drl0rscuf/video/upload/v1778795747/portfolio/videos/kura-pdp-cover-mp4.mp4",
      "assetPath": null,
      "caption": "Before there was a homepage, a listicle, or an advertorial, there was one product page.\n\nI started this portfolio with the hardest page to build well: the product page. It's the page that carries the most weight. It has to introduce the brand, agitate the problem, present the solution, prove it works, kill every objection, and ask for the sale, all without losing the reader halfway down.\n\nKURA's PDP follows a villain/hero structure. The \"villain\" section names the problem most people never think about: plastic boards that harbor bacteria, wood boards that crack and stain. Then the \"hero\" section introduces KURA as the upgrade, using 304 stainless steel that's non-porous and dishwasher safe.\n\nFrom there, a before/after comparison, a 3-step how-it-works block, review cards, three circular trust-stat indicators, a head-to-head comparison table against generic boards, an 8-question FAQ accordion, three trust pillars, and an email capture. Thirteen sections in total, each one a deliberate handoff to the next.\n\nThe buy box is sticky on desktop. Star rating sits above the product title. Price is impossible to miss. None of that is decoration. It's conversion architecture.\n\nBuilt in HTML/CSS/vanilla JS. No page builder. No theme.\n\nNeed a store like this built for your brand? DM me.\n\n#ecommerce #productpage #CRO #shopify #replo #webdesign #brandstrategy #uidesign",
      "hashtags": [],
      "status": "Not Posted",
      "postedAt": null,
      "note": "Cloudinary-hosted only, no local file. Product Page (PDP) cover video."
    },
